       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere are some common regimens you may have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a typical analgesic dose.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), often used for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, which may have been the intended total and not the per-dose amount.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy or an attending first."
