     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. Higher doses add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and they markedly increase the risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Entering it here could put it in front of nursing staff with no further check.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can place 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400 mg PO four times daily right now. The labeled maximum is 3,200 mg/day, for example 800 mg PO four times daily.\n- **Get a second opinion.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, talk to your attending or the pharmacist first. If they approve it, it should go through their channel with documentation of the rationale.\n- **Consider other options.** If pain control is the problem, I can help enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus an ibuprofen dose within range.\n\nTell me which one you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
